{"path":"numeric/complex/asin","title":"std::asin(std::complex)","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>asin<small>(std::complex)</small>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/numeric/complex/asin","section":"numeric","kind":"page","summary":"Computes complex arc sine of a complex value z. Branch cut exists outside the interval [−1, +1] along the real axis.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/complex\">&lt;complex&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx11\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">template</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span> <span class=\"kw1\">class</span> T <span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> asin<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>T<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> z <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(since C++11)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Computes complex arc sine of a complex value <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code>. Branch cut exists outside the interval <span class=\"texhtml\">[−1, +1]</span> along the real axis.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> z\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> complex value\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>If no errors occur, complex arc sine of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code> is returned, in the range of a strip unbounded along the imaginary axis and in the interval <span class=\"texhtml\">[−π/2, +π/2]</span> along the real axis.\n</p><p>Errors and special cases are handled as if the operation is implemented by <code>-i * <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/asinh\">std::asinh</a>(i * z)</code>, where <code>i</code> is the imaginary unit.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>Inverse sine (or arc sine) is a multivalued function and requires a branch cut on the complex plane. The branch cut is conventionally placed at the line segments <span class=\"texhtml\">(-∞,-1)</span> and <span class=\"texhtml\">(1,∞)</span> of the real axis.\n</p><p>The mathematical definition of the principal value of arc sine is <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small \\arcsin z = -{\\rm i}\\ln({\\rm i}z+\\sqrt{1-z^2})\">arcsin z = -<i>i</i>ln(<i>i</i>z + <span class=\"t-mrad\"><span>√</span><span>1-z<span class=\"t-su\">2<br></span></span></span>)</span>.\n</p>\nFor any <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">z</span></code>, <span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"\\small{ \\arcsin(z) = \\arccos(-z) - \\frac{\\pi}{2} }\">asin(z) = acos(-z) - <span class=\"t-mfrac\"><table><tr><td>π</td></tr><tr><td>2</td></tr></table></span></span>.\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;complex&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/manip/fixed\"><span class=\"kw1801\">std::<span class=\"me2\">fixed</span></span></a><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z1<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span>, <span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"asin\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z1 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/asin\"><span class=\"kw1344\">std::<span class=\"me2\">asin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z1<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z2<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">2.0</span>, <span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">0.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"asin\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" (the other side of the cut) = \"</span>\n              <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/asin\"><span class=\"kw1344\">std::<span class=\"me2\">asin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"co1\">// for any z, asin(z) = acos(−z) − pi / 2</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> pi <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw1345\">std::<span class=\"me2\">acos</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex\"><span class=\"kw1480\">std::<span class=\"me2\">complex</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">double</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> z3 <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/acos\"><span class=\"kw1345\">std::<span class=\"me2\">acos</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z2<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy2\">-</span> pi <span class=\"sy2\">/</span> <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"sin(acos\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> z2 <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" - pi / 2) = \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/sin\"><span class=\"kw1341\">std::<span class=\"me2\">sin</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>z3<span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>asin(-2.000000,0.000000) = (-1.570796,1.316958)\nasin(-2.000000,-0.000000) (the other side of the cut) = (-1.570796,-1.316958)\nsin(acos(-2.000000,-0.000000) - pi / 2) = (2.000000,0.000000)</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/acos\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>acos<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes arc cosine of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arccos{z}}\">arccos(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/atan\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>atan<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes arc tangent of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arctan{z}}\">arctan(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/complex/sin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>sin<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::complex)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes sine of a complex number (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\sin{z}}\">sin(z)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/asin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>asin</span><span>asinf</span><span>asinl</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  computes arc sine (<span class=\"mjax-fallback texhtml\" data-tex=\"{\\small\\arcsin{x}}\">arcsin(x)</span>) <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/valarray/asin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>asin<span class=\"t-dsc-small\">(std::valarray)</span></span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  applies the function <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/asin\">std::asin</a></span> to each element of valarray <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/numeric/complex/casin\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>casin</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"numeric","title":"Numerics library"},{"path":"numeric/complex","title":"std::complex"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::asin(std::complex)","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++11. Computes complex arc sine of a complex value z. Branch cut exists outside the interval [−1, +1] along the real axis."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"z"},{"label":"Return value","note":"If no errors occur, complex arc sine of z is returned, in the range of a strip unbounded along the imaginary axis and in the interval [−π/2, +π/2] along the…"},{"label":"Notes","note":"Inverse sine (or arc sine) is a multivalued function and requires a branch cut on the complex plane."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"acos(std::complex)","note":"computes arc cosine of a complex number (arccos(z))"},{"label":"atan(std::complex)","note":"computes arc tangent of a complex number (arctan(z))"},{"label":"sin(std::complex)","note":"computes sine of a complex number (sin(z))"},{"label":"asin, asinf, asinl","note":"computes arc sine (arcsin(x))"},{"label":"asin(std::valarray)","note":"applies the function std::asin to each element of valarray"}]}]},"standards":["C++11"],"wordCount":329,"codeBlockCount":2}
